{"seconds": 624.788, "paras": [{"n": 1, "start": 0.54, "end": 9.33, "text": "For twenty years, Dexter Morgan has been television's favour", "cut": 9.81}, {"n": 2, "start": 10.29, "end": 18.38, "text": "And right now, he's back. Dexter: Resurrection, season two, ", "cut": 18.86}, {"n": 3, "start": 19.34, "end": 30.9, "text": "But there's a question the show never really asks. What if D", "cut": 31.48}, {"n": 4, "start": 32.06, "end": 41.36, "text": "Because in real life, one crime lab chemist got more than tw", "cut": 42.09}, {"n": 5, "start": 42.82, "end": 53.31, "text": "Welcome to the Fiction Files. I'm your Detective. Every stor", "cut": 53.74}, {"n": 6, "start": 54.17, "end": 65.21, "text": "This case has three questions. One. Would Dexter's science e", "cut": 65.74}, {"n": 7, "start": 66.27, "end": 80.46, "text": "First, the fiction. Dexter began as a novel, Jeff Lindsay's ", "cut": 80.89}, {"n": 8, "start": 81.32, "end": 92.5, "text": "Dexter is a blood spatter analyst for the Miami Metro Police", "cut": 92.93}, {"n": 9, "start": 93.36, "end": 98.5, "text": "And the whole show rests on one idea. The man the system tru", "cut": 99.28}, {"n": 10, "start": 100.06, "end": 101.65, "text": "Exhibit A. The gatekeeper.", "cut": 102.18}, {"n": 11, "start": 102.71, "end": 113.62, "text": "In a real trial, an expert can't just walk in and give an op", "cut": 114.05}, {"n": 12, "start": 114.48, "end": 124.83, "text": "The older one comes from a 1923 case about an early lie dete", "cut": 125.26}, {"n": 13, "start": 125.69, "end": 136.3, "text": "The newer one comes from a 1993 Supreme Court case called Da", "cut": 136.73}, {"n": 14, "start": 137.16, "end": 156.56, "text": "Now here's the twist. Dexter works in Florida. And Florida c", "cut": 156.99}, {"n": 15, "start": 157.42, "end": 168.51, "text": "Which means that for almost the whole original run of the sh", "cut": 169.04}, {"n": 16, "start": 169.57, "end": 176.27, "text": "So, Exhibit A. Dexter's testimony walks straight in. But get", "cut": 177.1}, {"n": 17, "start": 177.93, "end": 179.78, "text": "Exhibit B. The science on the stand.", "cut": 180.31}, {"n": 18, "start": 180.84, "end": 197.59, "text": "Blood spatter analysis is real. In 1971, a criminalist calle", "cut": 198.02}, {"n": 19, "start": 198.45, "end": 217.93, "text": "By the time Dexter came along, it was a regular part of real", "cut": 218.46}, {"n": 20, "start": 218.99, "end": 232.77, "text": "In 2021, a study funded by the US National Institute of Just", "cut": 233.25}, {"n": 21, "start": 233.73, "end": 237.85, "text": "One in nine. And when that goes wrong in a courtroom, it can", "cut": 238.43}, {"n": 22, "start": 239.01, "end": 257.5, "text": "In 1985, in the small town of Clifton, Texas, a teacher name", "cut": 257.93}, {"n": 23, "start": 258.36, "end": 280.4, "text": "Joe Bryan was convicted. More than thirty years later, Texas", "cut": 281.03}, {"n": 24, "start": 281.66, "end": 301.16, "text": "Now, to be fair to Dexter. He isn't a detective with a short", "cut": 301.59}, {"n": 25, "start": 302.02, "end": 311.349, "text": "So, Exhibit B. The science is real. But it's nowhere near as", "cut": 312.179}, {"n": 26, "start": 313.009, "end": 315.499, "text": "Exhibit C. When the analyst is the criminal.", "cut": 316.029}, {"n": 27, "start": 316.559, "end": 329.399, "text": "But Dexter's biggest problem in court isn't the science. It'", "cut": 329.829}, {"n": 28, "start": 330.259, "end": 343.229, "text": "In 2012, investigators found that a chemist named Annie Dook", "cut": 343.659}, {"n": 29, "start": 344.089, "end": 358.679, "text": "When it came out, every case she had ever touched was sudden", "cut": 359.209}, {"n": 30, "start": 359.739, "end": 371.569, "text": "Then it happened again. Sonja Farak, a chemist at another st", "cut": 371.999}, {"n": 31, "start": 372.429, "end": 388.129, "text": "And the courts made the rules very clear. Prosecutors must h", "cut": 388.559}, {"n": 32, "start": 388.989, "end": 405.699, "text": "So picture the real version. The day Dexter is exposed, it i", "cut": 406.229}, {"n": 33, "start": 406.759, "end": 412.409, "text": "And for the record, we found no scandal like this at Miami D", "cut": 412.939}, {"n": 34, "start": 413.469, "end": 418.029, "text": "So, Exhibit C. Dexter's evidence might survive a courtroom. ", "cut": 418.859}, {"n": 35, "start": 419.689, "end": 421.029, "text": "Exhibit D. The clock.", "cut": 421.559}, {"n": 36, "start": 422.089, "end": 433.999, "text": "So, how long would Dexter really last? Let's start with the ", "cut": 434.429}, {"n": 37, "start": 434.859, "end": 445.579, "text": "And Miami is one of the hardest places to get caught. In Mia", "cut": 446.009}, {"n": 38, "start": 446.439, "end": 460.389, "text": "So for one crime, the odds are close to a coin flip. But Dex", "cut": 460.919}, {"n": 39, "start": 461.449, "end": 472.379, "text": "Of course, real cases aren't coin flips. Killers slip throug", "cut": 472.809}, {"n": 40, "start": 473.239, "end": 482.179, "text": "But here's what real cases show. Long running killers are ra", "cut": 482.659}, {"n": 41, "start": 483.139, "end": 493.639, "text": "In April 2018, investigators caught the Golden State Killer,", "cut": 494.069}, {"n": 42, "start": 494.499, "end": 501.869, "text": "Gary Ridgway, the Green River Killer, was caught in 2001, wh", "cut": 502.299}, {"n": 43, "start": 502.729, "end": 509.399, "text": "Israel Keyes was a careful killer who travelled across the c", "cut": 509.829}, {"n": 44, "start": 510.259, "end": 519.319, "text": "And in Gary, Indiana, a computer program written by a journa", "cut": 519.749}, {"n": 45, "start": 520.179, "end": 540.089, "text": "Now picture Miami today. DNA from a crime scene can be check", "cut": 540.519}, {"n": 46, "start": 540.949, "end": 561.039, "text": "And what about real people who did what Dexter does, and wen", "cut": 561.569}, {"n": 47, "start": 562.099, "end": 575.938, "text": "So how long would Dexter survive? Not decades. In my judgeme", "cut": 576.768}, {"n": 48, "start": 577.598, "end": 578.298, "text": "Time for the verdict.", "cut": 578.928}, {"n": 49, "start": 579.558, "end": 592.238, "text": "On the science. Blood spatter analysis is real, it's still u", "cut": 592.968}, {"n": 50, "start": 593.698, "end": 603.638, "text": "On the double life. No real person has done what Dexter does", "cut": 604.468}, {"n": 51, "start": 605.298, "end": 611.958, "text": "Which gives Dexter an overall reality score of... three out ", "cut": 612.788}, {"n": 52, "start": 613.618, "end": 622.838, "text": "Dexter: Resurrection's season finale lands on New Year's Day", "cut": 624.788}], "words": [["for", 0.59, 1], ["twenty", 0.88, 1], ["years", 0.95, 1], ["dexter", 1.27, 1], ["morgan", 1.63, 1], ["has", 2.0, 1], ["been", 2.21, 1], ["television's", 2.71, 1], ["favourite", 2.95, 1], ["killer", 3.2, 1], ["by", 4.05, 1], ["day", 4.22, 1], ["he", 4.45, 1], ["reads", 4.62, 1], ["blood", 4.95, 1], ["for", 5.29, 1], ["the", 5.52, 1], ["miami", 5.75, 1], ["police", 6.08, 1], ["by", 6.95, 1], ["night", 7.1, 1], ["he", 7.41, 1], ["hunts", 7.56, 1], ["the", 7.86, 1], ["killers", 8.07, 1], ["the", 8.48, 1], ["system", 8.68, 1], ["let", 9.03, 1], ["go", 9.24, 1], ["and", 10.3, 2], ["right", 10.48, 2], ["now", 10.76, 2], ["he's", 10.95, 2], ["back", 11.18, 2], ["dexter", 11.86, 2], ["resurrection", 12.84, 2], ["season", 14.02, 2], ["two", 14.35, 2], ["is", 14.41, 2], ["out", 14.59, 2], ["every", 14.83, 2], ["friday", 15.19, 2], ["all", 15.61, 2], ["the", 15.86, 2], ["way", 16.34, 2], ["to", 16.54, 2], ["the", 16.72, 2], ["finale", 16.96, 2], ["on", 17.38, 2], ["new", 17.56, 2], ["year's", 17.81, 2], ["day", 18.23, 2], ["but", 19.41, 3], ["there's", 19.58, 3], ["a", 19.91, 3], ["question", 19.99, 3], ["the", 20.37, 3], ["show", 20.53, 3], ["never", 20.74, 3], ["really", 20.99, 3], ["asks", 21.28, 3], ["what", 21.91, 3], ["if", 22.17, 3], ["dexter's", 22.33, 3], ["job", 22.79, 3], ["was", 23.0, 3], ["